id: pm-gh1676
title: "GH-1676: a pm close refused for missing close fields suggests a separate pm update and a retry, although pm close accepts --resolution, --expected-result and --actual-result itself"
description: "GitHub issue #1676 (reported 2026-11-06 against 2026.11.5). Reproduced 2026-11-06 on main af6fd5583 (2026.11.6) in a disposable non-git tracker: pm --no-extensions --pm-path .agents/pm close lab-one done --validate-close strict exits 2 with close_validation_missing_fields. The recovery bundle's suggested_retry is pm --pm-path .agents/pm --no-extensions update lab-one --resolution \"<value>\" --expected-result \"<value>\" --actual-result \"<value>\", and next_steps say \"Run the suggested pm update, then retry the original pm close invocation.\" pm close declares --resolution, --expected-result (alias --expected) and --actual-result (alias --actual) itself, so the single close call succeeds. Following the advertised route costs two writes, two history entries and two lock cycles, leaves a window where the item carries close evidence while still open, and moves updated_at (which reorders downstream changelog sections, unbraind/pm-changelog#323). GH-757 fixed the same class for pm update --status closed. Cause: collectCloseValidationWarnings in src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts renders an update command from commandScope, and the CLI recovery builder keeps a producer suggested_retry verbatim. Expected: suggested_retry and suggested_retry_args are the caller's own close invocation with each missing flag appended before any -- terminator (every other token, including tracker scope, --json and --expect-hash, preserved; an empty supplied value is replaced rather than duplicated), next_steps name that single command, and the update route stays as a secondary next_best_command. SDK callers without argv get a close command rendered from the item id, reason and command scope. Duplicate check: searched suggested_retry close refusal; pm-p316vn (GH-953, closed) preserved supplied flags for the close_reason path, pm-ulqu (GH-519, closed) fixed the enum placeholder, pm-5uclvd (GH-885, closed) fixed create-time close_reason_required. None covers the missing close-field refusal recommending a different command."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,close,"gh:1676",recovery,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-11-06T11:32:56.324Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T13:30:01.488Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-06T12:45:20.254Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-06T12:45:20.254Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A strict close refused for missing close fields returns suggested_retry and suggested_retry_args equal to the caller's own pm close invocation with each missing flag appended before any -- terminator, preserving tracker scope, --json and every other supplied token; An empty supplied close field (for example --resolution with an empty string, or its --expected/--actual alias) is replaced in the retry rather than duplicated; next_steps name the single pm close retry first and keep the pm update route only as a secondary next_best_command; SDK callers without an invocation argv receive a pm close command rendered from the item id, reason and command scope; A spec executes the emitted suggested_retry_args against a sandbox tracker and the item closes in one write with one history entry"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "The producer in src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts renders the retry as a pm close and keeps the pm update route as recovery.next_best_command. The new CLI repair src/cli/runtime/close-fields-retry.ts rebuilds suggested_retry and suggested_retry_args from the caller's exact argv with each missing flag inserted before any -- terminator. It is contract-aware: declared option values are consumed, and blank values under any alias are replaced. When the command cannot accept a field itself, or an option's arity is unknown, it keeps the producer's recovery."
expected_result: "suggested_retry is the same pm close plus the missing flags, preserving tracker scope, --json and --expect-hash. Replaying it closes the item in one write with one history entry."
actual_result: "Verified in a sandbox and by tests/integration/cli/recovery-replays-invocation.integration.spec.ts: the emitted suggested_retry_args, with values filled in, closed the item, and its history holds only create and close. 6 repair unit tests and the updated close-command spec pass. Disabling the repair fails the integration spec (negative control). Full suite 12112 passed, coverage 100/100/100/100."
